  "explanation": "<p>The four outcomes are graded by how much the combination gives you that you did not already have:</p><table class='xt'><tr><th><strong>outcome</strong></th><th><strong>what it means</strong></th></tr><tr><td>inconclusive</td><td>the modalities disagree and you cannot resolve it</td></tr><tr><td>dominated</td><td>one modality carries everything; the other is dead weight</td></tr><tr><td>modulated</td><td>one modality adjusts how the other is read</td></tr><tr><td><strong>emergent</strong></td><td><strong>a meaning appears that is in neither modality alone</strong></td></tr></table><p>Only <em>emergent</em> pays for the extra encoder, the extra data and the extra alignment problem. Sarcasm is the standard example: the words say one thing, the tone says another, and the meaning — irony — is in neither channel by itself.</p>",
