  "num": 11,
  "week": "W9",
  "explanation": "<p>Transfer learning is the general problem: reuse knowledge from a source setting in a target setting. Domain adaptation is the special case in which the <em>task</em> is held fixed and only the <em>domain</em> changes — classify the same categories, but on synthetic images instead of real ones. Narrowing the problem is what makes its specific tools (importance sampling, gradient reversal) applicable.</p>",
