  "explanation": "<p>Two independent axes: <em>how many parameters are trainable</em> and <em>how many bits each one takes</em>. LoRA moves the first, quantisation the second, and they compose.</p><table class='xt'><tr><th><strong>$7$B model</strong></th><th><strong>weights</strong></th><th><strong>grads</strong></th><th><strong>Adam</strong></th><th><strong>total</strong></th></tr><tr><td>(c) QLoRA, $8$-bit</td><td>$7$</td><td>$\\approx 0$</td><td>$\\approx 0$</td><td>$\\approx \\mathbf{7}$ GB</td></tr><tr><td>(a) LoRA, $16$-bit</td><td>$14$</td><td>$\\approx 0$</td><td>$\\approx 0$</td><td>$\\approx \\mathbf{14}$ GB</td></tr><tr><td>(d) full, $16$-bit</td><td>$14$</td><td>$14$</td><td>$28$</td><td>$\\mathbf{56}$ GB</td></tr><tr><td>(b) full, $32$-bit</td><td>$28$</td><td>$28$</td><td>$56$</td><td>$\\mathbf{112}$ GB</td></tr></table><p>The gap between (a) and (d) is a factor of four and comes entirely from the last three columns — exactly the bars deleted in the figure at Q13. Activations are omitted here because they depend on batch size and sequence length rather than on the method.</p>",
