  "exam": 3,
  "num": 6,
  "week": "W2",
  "explanation": "<p>Attention computes a weighted sum over all positions, and the weights depend only on the <em>content</em> of the vectors, never on where they sit. Permute the input tokens and the output permutes with them — the layer is permutation equivariant, so “the cat sat on the mat” and “the mat sat on the cat” are indistinguishable to it.</p><p><strong>The fix is to make position part of the content</strong>: add a vector that depends on the index, so two identical words at different positions arrive as different vectors.</p><p><strong>(b) is the trap</strong> — that is what the causal <em>mask</em> does (Q8), a different mechanism solving a different problem.</p>",
