  "explanation": "<p><strong>Filled in: For a convolution with kernel $K$, stride $S$, padding $P$ and no dilation, an input of size $H$ gives an output of size $\\mathbf{\\left\\lfloor (H + 2P - K)/S \\right\\rfloor + 1}$. A layer with $C_{\\text{in}}$ input channels, $C_{\\text{out}}$ output channels and a $K \\times K$ kernel has $\\mathbf{K^2 C_{\\text{in}} C_{\\text{out}}}$ weights and $\\mathbf{C_{\\text{out}}}$ biases.</strong> <strong>Read the output formula as a walk.</strong> $H + 2P$ is the padded length; you place the kernel at the far left, which consumes $K$ of it and is the “$+1$”; then you step by $S$ as many times as the remaining $H + 2P - K$ allows. The floor is where a stride that does not divide evenly quietly drops the last, incomplete window.</p><p><strong>One bias per output channel, not per position.</strong> That is weight sharing again: the same filter and the same bias are applied at every location, which is why the count does not mention $H$ or $W$ at all. See Q43 for the arithmetic on a real layer.</p>",
