  "week": "W3",
  "explanation": "<p>Patch size is fixed, so doubling $H$ and $W$ quadruples the number of tokens: $N = HW/P^2 \\to 4N$. Self-attention is $O(N^2d)$, and $(4N)^2 = 16N^2$.</p><p>The comparison is the reason this number matters. A convolution costs $O(HW\\,k^2C_{\\text{in}}C_{\\text{out}})$ — <em>linear</em> in pixels — so the same change costs a CNN $\\times 4$. Every doubling of resolution therefore moves a factor of four in the CNN's favour, and this single fact is why Swin exists.</p><p>Swin sits on the convolution's line, not the ViT's, because fixing the window at $M\\times M$ fixes the number of pairs <em>per window</em> and lets only the number of windows grow. The attention term becomes $2M^2hwC$ instead of $2(hw)^2C$, which is linear in patches.</p>",
